 {"id":"fabro-a0fe","title":"Tell develop reviewer to read blob refs with read_file offset/limit","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.015Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.630Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md (Input section, blob-ref paragraph), state that blob files are read with read_file (offset/limit for large blobs). reviewer@3 in run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V found python3/node unavailable and improvised nu str substring chunking on a 58.1 KB evidence blob because the prompt never mentions the sanctioned path. Expected effect: removes improvised-read friction; pairs with open seeds fabro-8d2c/fabro-d97b.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-ee2c","title":"Require ml record for implementer near-miss tool lessons","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.111Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.738Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 6 (or the stage-journal hook), make ml record mandatory for near-miss tool lessons. implementer@1's edit_file old_string swallowed a whole test loop body in fib_test.go, was caught only by re-reading, and the lesson went into the run journal that no future session loads; implementer@2 then spent 284 s / 0.49 USD (42% of run agent cost) editing the same 1,100-line table-literal file without the guardrail. Expected effect: the next implementer inherits the scoped-old_string guardrail via ml prime --files.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-169b","title":"Declare lesson_capture in the implementer node's context_allow_keys","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.461Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:24.008Z","description":"Seed fabro-f831 makes lesson_capture a required key of the Implemented JSON in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, but workflow.fabro's implementer node still declares context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,journal, so the undeclared key drops as drift on every future pass (per fabro-900e comment). Change: one line in workflow.fabro implementer node — context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,lesson_capture,journal; optionally also add it to the reviewer's preamble_allow_keys. Effect: the enforced record-or-skip answer lands durably instead of being discarded.","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:24.008Z","closeReason":"Closed 2026-09-05 triage: lesson_capture already declared in implementer context_allow_keys (workflow.fabro line 106)."}
-{"id":"fabro-3d2d","title":"Add a repo-layout map to the planner prompt or AGENTS.md","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.588Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T17:03:01.143Z","description":"planner@1 burned 354.7 s / $0.219 of the $0.547 total (50,460 input tokens) on ~10 exploratory calls just to locate dev-loop assets that live at .fabro/workflows/develop/ in the same repo; planner@2 with the layout in context took 98 s / $0.064. Change: add a short Repo layout / dev-loop assets subsection to AGENTS.md. CORRECTION (planner run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA, 2026-09-09): the original text said 'gofib at repo root' — stale repo name, this repo is fabro. AGENTS.md (real file; CLAUDE.md is a symlink to it) already has an '## Architecture' section covering lib/ and apps/ layout; the actual gap is dev-loop asset subpaths. Target: new subsection (e.g. '### Dev-loop assets') at the end of '## Architecture' in AGENTS.md listing: dev-loop workflow assets at .fabro/workflows/develop/ (prompts/, scripts/, schemas/, workflow.toml); reviews at .fabro/reviews/; stage journals at .fabro/journal/<run_id>.jsonl; seeds tracker at .seeds/ (sd CLI); expertise at .mulch/ (ml CLI). Note in the section that these paths are fs_hide-bound for file tools — shell reads (grep/cat/sed) work. Effect: first planner pass drops from ~6 min toward ~100 s — roughly −4.5 min wall and −$0.15 per run. Distinct from the sd call-economy seeds (fabro-e4fa/f4cd/1399): those tune tracker calls, this removes filesystem orientation calls.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
