 {"id":"fabro-4b57","title":"Emit a loop-work diff in evidence.nu when only churn files changed","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.453Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:28:39.799Z","description":"Seeds targeting .fabro/ paths are classified as loop churn by .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu, so captures read seed-work=0 files +0/-0 and reviewers must run their own git diff. Change: in evidence.nu, when seed_rows is empty but churn_rows is not, emit the per-seed (claim-base) diff of changed loop files under a loop-work diff section — the per-seed diff-base machinery from fabro-1e9f's theme already provides the base. Effect: reviews of dev-loop seeds verify from context, removing the per-review git detour. Cross-ref: fabro-1e9f (diff against last seed boundary) is the same machinery at run level.","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T16:28:39.799Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-a5de","title":"Ban sd prime in develop planner and implementer prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.627Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.941Z","description":"planner@1 executed sd prime because AGENTS.md memory instructs it, pulling a 4.7 KB banner whose Session Close Protocol mandates sd close + sd sync && git push — both reserved for the deterministic Closeout; the planner journaled that an LLM skimming the banner could comply. Change: one line in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md and prompts/implementer.md: never run sd prime in this loop — its close/push protocol contradicts the role rules and the context brief supersedes it. Effect: removes a directly contradicting instruction from every stage context and eliminates the mis-close/push risk. Complements the AGENTS.md boilerplate fix in fabro-cc23.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-3d04","title":"Make the authorized-exception pattern standing in the implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:49.669Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:38.038Z","description":"Briefs carry manual override prose (fabro-f831's brief opened with CONTRADICTION RESOLVED authorizing exactly one .fabro/ file), and implementer@2 journaled that the pattern recurred across fabro-7e44 and fabro-f831 and deserves a platform-level convention. Change: in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md's Platform scope section add: exception — a brief that names a specific platform file authorizes editing exactly that file. Effect: planner briefs shed roughly a third of their text and the implementer no longer reconciles a contradiction before starting.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
